From 7466ca1634b0dc9e9171e3c476ed703409853e46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Michaud <jmichaud@igalia.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:52:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] [mya] Add a `refs` command to find what holds an
 address range Need the bug URL (OOPS!).

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

`refs <start> <end>` lists every word of the current snapshot's writable
memory whose value lies in [start, end), with the region it is in (and, on
Darwin, the region's VM tag): what holds an allocation, for instance one the
heap walk reports as missed. Memory the target cannot write holds no address
it allocated, so read-only regions are skipped, and only the resident parts
of each region are read, so large untouched reservations cost nothing. It
lists the first 200 and counts the rest.

Independent of the heap walk: it needs only the region list.

* Source/JavaScriptCore/mya/mya.cpp:

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Source/JavaScriptCore/mya/mya.cpp | 111 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
